%I A119864 #35 Aug 06 2026 00:01:36
%S A119864 12,200,702,890,1382,1392,1580,2082,2270,2764,2772,2960,3462,3650,
%T A119864 4146,4152,4340,4842,5030,5528,5532,5720,6222,6410,6910,6912,7100,
%U A119864 7602,7790,8292,8480,8982,9170,9672,9674,9860,10362,10550,11052,11056,11240,11742
%N A119864 Numbers m such that the numerator of BernoulliB(m) is divisible by 691.
%C A119864 This sequence is the union of the three arithmetic progressions 12 + 690*k (k >= 0), 200 + 690*k (k >= 0) and 2*691*k (k >= 1), with the multiples of 476790 = 690*691 removed: 690 divides such a number, so by the von Staudt-Clausen theorem 691 divides the denominator of the corresponding Bernoulli number and therefore does not divide its numerator. [Corrected by _Qiyuan Gu_, Jul 29 2026]
%C A119864 Note that the numerator of BernoulliB(8292) is divisible by 691^2, where 8292 = 12 + 690*12 = 691*12. Also, the numerator of BernoulliB(138200) is also divisible by 691^2, where 138200 = 200 + 690*200 = 691*200.
%H A119864 Qiyuan Gu, <a href="/A119864/b119864.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..3448</a> (terms up to 2*690*691)
%H A119864 Bernd C. Kellner, <a href="https://www.bernoulli.org/">The Bernoulli number page</a>.
%H A119864 <a href="/index/Rec#order_1725">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, order 1725.
%F A119864 a(n+1724) = a(n) + 476790. - _Qiyuan Gu_ and _Jianing Song_, Jul 29 2026
%F A119864 a(n) = a(n-1) + a(n-1724) - a(n-1725) for n >= 1726. - _Qiyuan Gu_, Jul 29 2026
%e A119864 The sequence of Bernoulli numbers begins 1, -1/2, 1/6, 0, -1/30, 0, 1/42, 0, -1/30, 0, 5/66, 0, -691/2730, 0, 7/6, 0, -3617/510, ... 12 is a term because the numerator of BernoulliB(12) is 691.
%t A119864 With[{nmax = 30}, t = {Table[2n*691, {n, 1, nmax}], Table[12 + 690*n, {n, 0, nmax}], Table[200 + 690*n, {n, 0, nmax}]}; Select[Union[Join @@ t], # <= Min[Last /@ t] && !Divisible[#, 690*691] &]] (* edited by _Amiram Eldar_, Jul 31 2026 *)
%t A119864 (* Alternative: *)
%t A119864 Select[Range[2,12000,2],Divisible[Numerator[BernoulliB[#]],691]&] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Nov 19 2014 *)
%o A119864 (PARI) isA119864(k) = k%690==12 || k%690==200 || (k%1382==0 && k%476790!=0) \\ _Jianing Song_, Jul 29 2026
%Y A119864 Cf. A027641.
%K A119864 nonn,easy
%O A119864 1,1
%A A119864 _Alexander Adamchuk_, Jul 31 2006
